From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:06:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(settings): monitor drag keeps the layout gap-free and
 refuses overlapping drops

Problem: the layout canvas only snapped within 12 px of an edge, so a drop elsewhere left a gap; moving a monitor that joined two others left the rest disconnected; edge maths ignored the monitor scale; the canvas rescaled mid-drag.
Fix: monitor-layout.js lays out the whole canvas on each drag step. The dropped monitor attaches to its nearest neighbour, sharing at least a quarter of the shorter edge, with edges within the snap threshold lined up. Every detached group is pulled onto it, nearest first; a group holding a Nix-locked monitor stays and the other side moves. A drop overlapping another monitor by more than the threshold shows red and is refused. logicalWidth/logicalHeight divide by scale. All moved monitors go through one krane-ii-settings try (try monitor A ... + B ...).
